  <model metaid="meta_tirzepatide_liver" id="tirzepatide_liver" name="Model for the biliary excretion of the tirzepatide metabolites." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for the biliary excretion of the tirzepatide metabolites</h1>
        <p>The metabolites of tirzepatide are taken up from the plasma of the liver
and excreted into the bile, i.e. into the intestinal lumen, in one step
(<code>TMBEX</code>); the amounts in the hepatocytes and the bile are not resolved.
Tirzepatide itself is not excreted in the bile (Martin2024: no intact
tirzepatide in urine or feces).</p>
        <p>
          <strong>version</strong> 2</p>
